 in other words he likes to  show his physical prowess he's going to  do an ironman maybe  uh approach to today you know um stretch  it out there will be a lot of  gamesmanship but i thought  word of the adversary was quite  interesting too because the president's  been criticized for giving putin a  meeting as if it's some kind of prize  and to be called a word the adversary by  an american president for putin who  wants  to look on parity with an american  president is a kind of  gift in advance of this form of respect  in some ways exactly  which means when they get behind closed  doors you would expect perhaps the  president to say look i  i've shown you respect there here are  the things you need to hear me on  in this private way uh sort of playing  an inside game and announcement there's  a meeting going on but there are  parameters for the meeting as we  understand it the men will be together  for hours along with staff but  no meal will be shared they will never  be alone together and then afterwards  there will be no joint press conference  that's a lot of choreography why  it is well and think about the last time  that a president met with vladimir putin  when president trump met with him  it was the exact opposite it was  unscripted it was harem scarum it was  not as tightly controlled and the reason  it has to be tightly controlled again  is to make sure there are no  misunderstandings that both sides need  to know exactly what they're saying to  each other  and that's just that's about the moment  but it's also for six months from now  so that when vladimir putin is making  choices about what he's going to do  he can have in his mind the recollection  of what they said in those meetings and  the same is true for the for president  biden as well  and so you just it has to be  choreographed so that there's no  misunderstanding because  inside the misunderstanding is where you  have things go wrong now president biden  has been on quite the trip  of the tour of europe what is the  significance you think of this coming on  the heels of the g7  and nato where a unified front was  presented so president ryden keeps  saying and all this stuff keeps saying  america is back  what does that mean it means that the  president is putting himself forward  as the kind of the lead spokesman for a  whole set of values that basically  established the liberal order  in international relations over the last  70 80 years  so it's not just u.s russia relations  it's president biden saying i am here as  the representative of the most powerful  democracy on the planet  and here's what we believe and these  aren't just abstract notions  i have countries behind me i have the  nato alliance behind me  and that gives force to what i say that  is both a public message  but it's also private i mean when i  asked dr condoleeza rice the former  secretary of state how to measure this  she said don't look at the pageantry  watch six months later if the private  messages have paid off  what would we look for lower fewer cyber  attacks  maybe some improvement on the human  rights front  but those private messages are going to  be the most interesting and unfortunate  we won't learn about those for about six  months or so  john we're looking as you're speaking at  president biden's motorcade on its way  to the meeting with  president putin what how successful has  president biden been so far do you think  on this trip and  and what constitutes success in this  meeting with vladimir putin yeah  well that's a great point we'll start  with putin as i was saying about  former secretary rice her point was  success is  if he can convey in these private  meetings this is what is important in  the united states and  this is what we know you're up to he can  president  biden can talk about intelligence and  about what the u.s really knows the  russians are up to and can say  if you keep going down this road here is  the retaliation you can expect  again predictability because in  misunderstanding you can have a real  particularly with cyber it can go  haywire fast so  unfortunately a lot of that we won't be  able to measure in the moment and we  might not be able to measure  four months part of evaluating the  president's performance will be what did  vladimir putin get out of this so  what does putin hope to bring home to  russia politically what does he need to  do or want to do here  well he's already brought it home which  is being called a worthy adversary as  anthony mentioned by the u.s president  he wants to look like  he wants to be able to say look i can  meddle in ukraine i can  imprison my political opponents and i  pay no penalty for it so strength works  now the white house knows that they know  they're giving him that little bit  but what they've made the calculation is  it's worth giving  putin that because what we want is  clarity and we want him to stop behaving  in the way  he is and the only way we can get a shot  at doing that is if we deliver these  messages privately to him but doesn't  putin still need the united states for  his home audience and say look there's  the big enemy out there they're enemy  number one i've kept you safe keep me in  power for another decade  sure he one foot on the gas one front of  the break so he'll say  they're the big enemy out there i am the  only one who can stand up to them but  when i do  i get this parody i get uh called a  worthy adversary and so  he can um put show some of those  bouquets that he's gotten  you know and so in that sense he wants  to look like he is  um chummy with the american president  that's chummy goes too far  but looks like he can um uh he's close  be at least uh on well on the same level  with an american president  which is um which is one that that  allows him to show look i can do both  things  for you the russian people so all of  this is happening as alexi navalny is in  prison in russia how does that play into  this  especially 